title: The Reckoning
subtitle: The Central Committee meets to decide who failed in 1923, and who leads in 1924.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1923 and month = 12 and e23_reckoning = 0 and crisis = 0 and congress = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 2
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.e22) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.e22_lib.onArrival); }
RG.e22.leader();
Q.e23_right_blamed = (Q.lead_code == 3 && (Q.german_october == 1 || Q.german_october == 2)) ? 1 : 0;
Q.e23_rk_moscow_left = (Q.moscow_backs == 'offensive') ? 1 : 0;
Q.e23_rk_three = (Q.unionist_gone == 0 && Q.offensive_gone == 0 && Q.luxemburgist_gone == 0) ? 1 : 0;
Q.e23_rk_backing = 0;
!}

= The Reckoning

[? if kpd_banned = 1 : The Central Committee meets in a flat in Lichtenberg with two comrades on the stairs and a third at the tram stop. ?][? if kpd_banned = 0 : The Central Committee meets in the Zentrale's offices on the Rosenthaler Strasse, with a police car parked opposite. ?] There is one item on the agenda, the lessons of 1923.

[? if german_october = 1 : The rising was called off at Chemnitz and Hamburg fought alone. Fischer's people say the Zentrale lost its nerve and left Thälmann's men to be shot. Brandler's people say the retreat saved the party. ?][? if german_october = 2 : The rising was fought and lost. The Left says hesitation lost it. The Right says it should never have been called. ?][? if german_october = 3 : The councils hold Berlin, and the Central Committee is arguing about the next stage. Some of the delegates have come straight from the barricades. ?][? if german_october = 0 and e23_october_done = 1 : The party did not rise. Half the room thinks it missed the chance of a generation, and the other half thinks that is why there is still a party. ?][? if german_october = 0 and e23_october_done = 0 : There was no October in Germany. The party spent the year in strikes and committees, and the Left says that is all it will ever do. ?]

[? if e23_right_blamed = 1 : Brandler and Thalheimer led the Zentrale through the October, and fewer districts stand by them each week. ?][? if e23_rk_moscow_left = 1 : The Executive has let it be known that it wants the Left to lead. ?][? if e23_quarrel = 2 : Everyone knows that our delegates in Moscow voted to condemn the leaders of the October. ?][? if e23_quarrel = 1 : Our delegates in Moscow stood by Radek and the retreat. ?] [? if e23_rk_three = 1 : Pieck, Remmele and Eberlein have formed a middle group between the two camps. ?]

- @right: Put our name to Brandler's resolution.
- @left: Put our name to the Left's resolution.
- @middle: Put our name to the middle group's resolution.

@right
subtitle: The retreat was right, and the united front goes on. [? if e23_right_blamed = 1 : The room is against him. ?]
view-if: unionist_gone = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.e23_rk_backing = 'unionist';
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

- @open: The Central Committee meets.

@left
subtitle: The Zentrale failed the revolution. Moscow will probably agree.
view-if: offensive_gone = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.e23_rk_backing = 'offensive';
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
if (Q.leading_faction != 'offensive') { Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 6; }
!}

- @open: The Central Committee meets.

@middle
subtitle: Both camps were wrong. It needs one of them to come over.
view-if: luxemburgist_gone = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.e23_rk_backing = 'luxemburgist';
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 2;
if (Q.leading_faction != 'luxemburgist') { Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 4; }
!}

- @open: The Central Committee meets.

@open
title: The Central Committee in Session
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
RG.congressStart({
    id: 'reckoning',
    name: 'The Central Committee',
    stake: 'The lessons of 1923, and who leads into 1924',
    sessions: 2,
    positions: ['unionist', 'offensive', 'luxemburgist'],
    backing: Q.e23_rk_backing,
    kind: 'leadership',
    mandates: 'zentrale',
    delegates: 120,
    ownClose: true
});
if (Q.congress_reckoning == 1) {
    var C = RG.congress;
    if (Q.e23_right_blamed == 1 && Q.offensive_gone == 0) { C.swayTo('offensive', 0.08); }
    if (Q.german_october == 0 && Q.e23_october_done == 1 && Q.unionist_gone == 0) { C.swayTo('unionist', 0.04); }
    if (Q.german_october == 2 && Q.lead_code == 2 && Q.luxemburgist_gone == 0) { C.swayTo('luxemburgist', 0.06); }
    if (Q.e23_hh_rises == 1 && Q.german_october == 1 && Q.offensive_gone == 0) { C.swayTo('offensive', 0.04); }
    if (Q.e23_cuno_result == 1 && Q.unionist_gone == 0) { C.swayTo('unionist', 0.03); }
    if (Q.e23_quarrel == 2 && Q.offensive_gone == 0) { C.swayTo('offensive', 0.04); }
    if (Q.e23_quarrel == 1 && Q.unionist_gone == 0) { C.swayTo('unionist', 0.03); }
    if (Q.e23_oct_martyr_ok == 1) { C.bitter(4); }
    C.tally();
}
!}

= The Central Committee in Session

Forty members of the Central Committee and the district secretaries sit around three tables pushed together. The Zentrale votes as a body. [? if congress_ahead = 1 : The first soundings give our resolution [+ congress_votes_for +] per cent. ?][? if congress_ahead = 0 and congress_votes_for > 0 : The first soundings give the [+ congress_leader_name +] [+ congress_leader_votes +] per cent, and our resolution [+ congress_votes_for +]. ?][? if congress_ahead = 0 and congress_votes_for = 0 : The first soundings give the [+ congress_leader_name +] [+ congress_leader_votes +] per cent, and our resolution would fall on the first ballot. ?]

There will be two sittings before the vote.
